 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? That's a common problem. Try starting with the nose, then the brow, then the eyes. Use small, quick strokes, going from light to dark. You can always add more. Start near the nose, then work out. It' easier to darken than to lighten. Start at the corner, and keep the line thin. It should look like a little mountain. Practice makes difference. Try a face or two every day. Fun. Draw the shape of a person from the side, then fill in the details. It' like a puzzle, and you see the whole thing come together.",
